Meetings gain a lifecycle owner: `POST /meetings` (V19) takes an optional `externally_managed_by` text field (e.g. `"google_calendar"`, `"outlook"`; absent/null = wire-managed; echoed in meeting responses; immutable after creation, not part of updates). Externally-managed meetings can only be created, updated, deleted, link-refreshed and have invitations changed by calendar-integration (OAuth) callers presenting `Z-Client: Calendar`; Wire clients (cookie/token with a connection) get `403 externally-managed-by-calendar`. Inconsistent pairing (calendar fields or the header on a wire-managed request, missing header/calendar fields on an externally-managed create) returns `400 invalid-op`. Meeting mutation routes now accept OAuth bearer callers (connection header is optional), enabling pure-bearer clients such as the calendar add-on.

Externally-managed creates additionally carry `externally_calendar_event_id` and `externally_calendar_id` (nullable text, persisted, immutable). Creating an externally-managed meeting on a deployment whose license does not cover calendar integration returns `403 id-feature-error`. Externally-managed meetings send no emails through Wire.
